Preserve sharing while closing dependency strata

Close ordinary rule components in dependency order inside the existing
outer allocation loop, so downstream rules can consume completed inputs.
Keep simultaneous scheduling as the default, with dependency scheduling
opt-in while its maintenance costs are improved.

Analyze dependencies on flattened rule groups before RAM lowering and
carry the resulting schedule with the RAM program, so code generation
only emits the selected execution order.

Give each consuming component checkpoints of shared published relation
versions. Preserve roots across unchanged storage rebuilds and unchanged
subtrees across edits, and keep equality replacements visible as new
work.

Retain deferred definition requests across early close_until returns so
resumption cannot lose work whose premises were already consumed.

Compare scheduling modes alongside evaluation and morphism modes, and
cover nested allocation feedback, recursive strata, equality joins, and
physical snapshot sharing. Model-instance scheduling remains future
work.
